error[E0277]: `[u8; 32]` has not opted in to cloning, so a secret wrapping it cannot be cloned
  --> tests/compile-fail/newtype_derive_clone_attr_slot.rs:25:14
   |
25 |     #[derive(Clone)]
   |              ^^^^^ `[u8; 32]` does not implement `CloneableSecret`
   |
   = help: the trait `CloneableSecret` is not implemented for `[u8; 32]`
   = note: Cloning a secret makes a second full copy in memory, and every copy then has to be zeroized. This crate will not make that decision for you, so `Clone` on `Fixed` and `Dynamic` is gated behind this marker instead of being derived.
   = note: For a type you define, add an empty `impl CloneableSecret` block for it, next to its `Zeroize` impl. Like this crate's other markers it is an assertion the compiler cannot check: you are saying the inner type's `Clone` yields a value whose own zeroization is equally sound.
   = note: For a type you do not own, the orphan rule forbids that impl and rejects it with E0117 — wrap it in a newtype of your own and implement the marker for that.
   = note: If you arrived here from `#[derive(Clone)]` on a generated newtype, the derive forwards to the wrapper's `Clone`, which is what requires this marker. The `derive: [Clone]` argument is refused outright with a fuller explanation; writing `impl Clone` by hand keeps the decision visible in your own code.
   = note: required for `Fixed<[u8; 32]>` to implement `Clone`
   = note: this error originates in the derive macro `Clone` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)
